{"source":"jd2025.pdf","page":2,"pageWidth":612,"pageHeight":792,"items":[{"text":"bilateral ICA disease. In patients with chronic ICA occlusion,","rect":[72.3118,377.9206,299.87101591000004,386.40189999999996],"fontSize":8.4813},{"text":"collateral pathways, extending beyond the circle of Willis and pial","rect":[72.3118,366.44624923,299.87695282000016,374.92754922999995],"fontSize":8.4813},{"text":"arteries, can also involve intracranial-extracranial arterial","rect":[72.3118,354.97189846,299.75058144999997,363.45319845999995],"fontSize":8.4813},{"text":"anastomoses.","rect":[72.3118,343.49754769,120.96308119000004,351.97884768999995],"fontSize":8.4813},{"text":"2","rect":[121.0225,346.989,124.3691212,352.4769],"fontSize":6.4857},{"text":"Of these, ophthalmic artery collateral vessels are","rect":[126.5263,343.4967,299.7356492500001,351.97799999999995],"fontSize":8.4813},{"text":"recognized as particularly common.","rect":[72.31128601000002,332.02234923,195.97457692,340.50364922999995],"fontSize":8.4813},{"text":"UHR PCCTA holds significant clinical value in complex cerebro-","rect":[87.27823612000002,320.54799846,299.86202061999995,329.02929845999995],"fontSize":8.4813},{"text":"vascular disease. In patients with chronic ICA occlusion,","rect":[72.31128601000002,309.07364769,299.7424342900001,317.55494768999995],"fontSize":8.4813},{"text":"ECA-derived collateral vessels are crucial but often underesti-","rect":[311.7833359,377.92144856999994,539.295904659999,386.4027485699999],"fontSize":8.4813},{"text":"mated by DSA. UHR PCCTA, with its superior spatial resolution,","rect":[311.7833359,366.44709779999994,517.9951197099988,374.9283977999999],"fontSize":8.4813},{"text":"3","rect":[517.8585,369.9383,521.1532356,375.42620000000005],"fontSize":6.4857},{"text":"iden-","rect":[522.117,366.446,539.5375901999998,374.9273],"fontSize":8.4813},{"text":"tified critical ECA collateral vessels, guiding ECA angioplasty and lead-","rect":[311.78160813,354.97164923,539.5460714999992,363.45294923],"fontSize":8.4813},{"text":"ing to symptom improvement. This technology shows great potential","rect":[311.78160813,343.49729846,539.5053612599986,351.97859846],"fontSize":8.4813},{"text":"for preoperative planning and postoperative evaluation in patients","rect":[311.78160813,332.02294769,539.3382796499997,340.50424769],"fontSize":8.4813},{"text":"with chronic ICA occlusion, such as Moyamoya disease, where com-","rect":[311.78160813,320.54859692,539.3832305399998,329.02989692],"fontSize":8.4813},{"text":"prehensive collateral vessel assessment is critical.","rect":[311.78160813,309.07424615,482.4474155099998,317.55554615],"fontSize":8.4813},{"text":"ARTICLE INFORMATION","rect":[72.3118,282.0076,143.59453222000002,288.9922],"fontSize":6.9846},{"text":"Author Affiliations:","rect":[72.3118,270.03390022,130.2909646,277.01850022],"fontSize":6.9846},{"text":"Department of Radiology,","rect":[131.57752792000002,270.03390022,204.88858798000007,277.01850022],"fontSize":6.9846},{"text":"Ruijin Hospital, Shanghai Jiao Tong University","rect":[72.3118,261.0538,201.50035852000002,268.0384],"fontSize":6.9846},{"text":"School of Medicine, Shanghai, China (He, Yan);","rect":[72.3118,252.07369978000003,204.34937685999998,259.05829978],"fontSize":6.9846},{"text":"Department of Neurosurgery, Ruijin Hospital,","rect":[72.3118,243.09359956000003,200.96883046,250.07819956000003],"fontSize":6.9846},{"text":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University School of Medicine,","rect":[72.3118,234.11349934000003,214.42466236,241.09809934000003],"fontSize":6.9846},{"text":"Shanghai, China (Jiang).","rect":[72.3118,225.13339912000004,140.71198780000003,232.11799912000004],"fontSize":6.9846},{"text":"Corresponding Author:","rect":[72.3118,213.15969934000003,141.94407124000003,220.14429934000003],"fontSize":6.9846},{"text":"Hong Jiang, MD, PhD,","rect":[143.25927142,213.15969934000003,204.88649260000003,220.14429934000003],"fontSize":6.9846},{"text":"Ruijin Hospital, Shanghai Jiao Tong Univers